{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"elf_caravan_wagon","model_identifier":"elf_caravan_wagon","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"## elf_caravan_wagon\n\nElf caravan wagon (E6).\n\n- Cubes: 100 (24 rotated). Texture 256x512, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Bounds at rest: x -29.0..29.0, y 0.0..69.0, z -154.2..75.0 (size 58.0 x 69.0 x 229.2 u = 163 x 194 x 645 cm).\nElf caravan wagon: a long, graceful covered wagon (body 4 m = 142 u including the back crates; 229 u with the pole) in pale ash with carved scroll-work sides, sweeping upturned rail ends, white marble trim on the four corners, a hooped green cloth canopy with a pale leaf pattern, two hanging lanterns (front and back; `glow_*` cores), a driver's bench, stacked crates on the back step and four tall four-spoke wheels (0.9 m) with silver-grey tyres. Each side is a hinged panel (with a team-colour stripe) that folds down into a market-stall counter showing food crates, fruit, bread and cloth-wrapped blades. Pulled by two horses abreast or one tamed bear on a central pole. Faces -Z.\n\n**Hit box:** one box 58 x 69 x 140 u from y = 0, centred x = 0, z = 2 (body; the pole is not solid). With the stall open the width becomes 87 u.\n\n**Bones:** `root` > `body` (pivot on the axle line) > `panel_r` / `panel_l` (hinges along the bottom outer edges, 29 u up), `pole`, `lantern_f` / `lantern_b` (hooks under the canopy ends); `wheel_fr/fl/br/bl` on `root`.\n\n**Slots:** `slot_hitch` at the pole tip (44 u up, 154 u ahead), where the yoke meets the collars of two horses (or one bear's harness); `slot_rider` / `slot_rider_2` on the driver's bench (hips at 41 u); `slot_crew_1` / `slot_crew_2` = the traders' stall positions beside the open counters (48 u out on each side).\n\n**Move speed:** `move` designed for 35.6 u/s (1.0 m/s): one wheel turn per 2.82 s (circumference 100.5 u); the lanterns swing and the body bobs.\n\n**Key times:** `open` 2.0 s: both side panels fold down to horizontal counters at counter height (29 u = 82 cm), settling with a small bounce; key 1.5 s (stall open, trading can start). Play `open` reversed to close. `idle` lanterns sway. `damaged` 0.7 s shudder, a wheel wobbles, the lanterns jerk and a panel bangs. `destroyed` holds: both right wheels break off flat, the wagon slumps hard onto its broken right side (about 15 degrees), the panels burst open, the lanterns swing out and the pole drops.\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop |\n|---|---|---|\n| `idle` | 4 | loop |\n| `move` | 2.824 | loop |\n| `open` | 2 | once |\n| `damaged` | 0.7 | once |\n| `destroyed` | 1.8 | hold |\n"},"description":"## elf_caravan_wagon\n\nElf caravan wagon (E6).\n\n- Cubes: 100 (24 rotated). Texture 256x512, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Bounds at rest: x -29.0..29.0, y 0.0..69.0, z -154.2..75.0 (size 58.0 x 69.0 x 229.2 u = 163 x 194 x 645 cm).\nElf caravan wagon: a long, graceful covered wagon (body 4 m = 142 u including the back crates; 229 u with the pole) in pale ash with carved scroll-work sides, sweeping upturned rail ends, white marble trim on the four corners, a hooped green cloth canopy with a pale leaf pattern, two hanging lanterns (front and back; `glow_*` cores), a driver's bench, stacked crates on the back step and four tall four-spoke wheels (0.9 m) with silver-grey tyres. Each side is a hinged panel (with a team-colour stripe) that folds down into a market-stall counter showing food crates, fruit, bread and cloth-wrapped blades. Pulled by two horses abreast or one tamed bear on a central pole. Faces -Z.\n\n**Hit box:** one box 58 x 69 x 140 u from y = 0, centred x = 0, z = 2 (body; the pole is not solid). With the stall open the width becomes 87 u.\n\n**Bones:** `root` > `body` (pivot on the axle line) > `panel_r` / `panel_l` (hinges along the bottom outer edges, 29 u up), `pole`, `lantern_f` / `lantern_b` (hooks under the canopy ends); `wheel_fr/fl/br/bl` on `root`.\n\n**Slots:** `slot_hitch` at the pole tip (44 u up, 154 u ahead), where the yoke meets the collars of two horses (or one bear's harness); `slot_rider` / `slot_rider_2` on the driver's bench (hips at 41 u); `slot_crew_1` / `slot_crew_2` = the traders' stall positions beside the open counters (48 u out on each side).\n\n**Move speed:** `move` designed for 35.6 u/s (1.0 m/s): one wheel turn per 2.82 s (circumference 100.5 u); the lanterns swing and the body bobs.\n\n**Key times:** `open` 2.0 s: both side panels fold down to horizontal counters at counter height (29 u = 82 cm), settling with a small bounce; key 1.5 s (stall open, trading can start). Play `open` reversed to close. `idle` lanterns sway. `damaged` 0.7 s shudder, a wheel wobbles, the lanterns jerk and a panel bangs. `destroyed` holds: both right wheels break off flat, the wagon slumps hard onto its broken right side (about 15 degrees), the panels burst open, the lanterns swing out and the pole drops.\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop |\n|---|---|---|\n| `idle` | 4 | loop |\n| `move` | 2.824 | loop |\n| `open` | 2 | once |\n| `damaged` | 0.7 | once |\n| `destroyed` | 1.8 | hold |\n","resolution":{"width":256,"height":512},"elements":[{"name":"floor","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-22.0,26.0,-64.0],"to":[22.0,29.0,64.0],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[0.0,16.0,0.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[116,366,160.0,369.0],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[52,353,180.0,356.0],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[160,366,204.0,369.0],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[0,357,128.0,360.0],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[0,0,44.0,128.0],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[44,0,88.0,128.0],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"23960124-c553-5305-85e9-67111b058a35"},{"name":"sill_r","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[20.0,22.0,-60.0],"to":[2